This PR is a first MVP-level implementation of MCP service for neuro-san.
Tested by running an agent using MCP tool through Langchain MCP adapter, MCP server for this tool being neuro-san instance itself. We used both separate neuro-san instance and also the same one.
Things to note:

1. MCP service implements (kinda) latest 2026-06-18 protocol, in partial subset;
2. MCP service always runs - when neuro-san runs http service, MCP endpoint is also available for the same set of agent networks;
3. Since MCP payload is a JSON-RPC structure, we have actually a single Tornado-level handler, dispatching various MCP requests to different internal functions;
4. Underlying sessions we use are async;
5. True streaming http requests are not yet implemented, "tool/call" request returns a single result from chat request stream: message(s) of type AGENT_FRAMEWORK;
6. All incoming MCP requests are validated against published protocol schema, which is pretty convenient - if validation passed, you know exactly what you are dealing with at least format-wise.

## Overview

This PR extends the shadow note preview feature in note input mode to display a preview note with staff lines when the mouse cursor is positioned to the right of the last measure. Previously, no preview was shown in this area, making it unclear where notes would be placed.

## Problem

In note input mode, `NotationInteraction::showShadowNote` displays a preview note at the cursor position within measures. However, when the cursor moved beyond the last measure's right edge, no preview appeared because:

1. `Score::searchMeasure()` returned `nullptr` for positions beyond all measures
2. `Score::getPosition()` failed and returned `false`
3. The shadow note was hidden, leaving users without visual feedback

## Solution

The implementation adds four focused changes to enable preview rendering beyond the last measure:

### 1. Measure Detection (`Score::searchMeasure`)
Modified to return the last measure in a system when the cursor is beyond all measures, instead of returning `nullptr`:

```cpp
Measure* lastMeasure = nullptr;
for (MeasureBase* mb : system->measures()) {
    if (mb->isMeasure()) {
        if (x < (mb->x() + mb->ldata()->bbox().width())) {
            return toMeasure(mb);
        }
        lastMeasure = toMeasure(mb);
    }
}
if (lastMeasure) {
    return lastMeasure;  // Return last measure if beyond all measures
}
```

### 2. Position Calculation (`Score::getPosition`)
Modified to allow positioning beyond the last segment of a measure, preserving the actual cursor x-coordinate:

```cpp
if (ns == nullptr) {
    // Allow positioning beyond the last segment
    if (x >= x1) {
        pos->segment = segment;
        break;
    }
    // ... existing fallback code
}
```

### 3. Staff Lines Flag (`ShadowNote`)
Added a boolean flag to track when staff lines should be drawn:

```cpp
bool drawStaffLines() const { return m_drawStaffLines; }
void setDrawStaffLines(bool draw) { m_drawStaffLines = draw; }
```

### 4. Visual Rendering (`TDraw::draw` for ShadowNote)
Added staff line rendering when the shadow note is beyond the last measure:

```cpp
if (item->drawStaffLines()) {
    // Draw all staff lines (typically 5) around the note position
    for (int i = 0; i < numLines; ++i) {
        double y = (i - item->lineIndex()) * lineDistance;
        painter->drawLine(LineF(x1, y, x2, y));
    }
}
```

Staff lines extend 2 spatiums on each side of the note for clear visibility and use the same positioning formula as ledger lines: `y = (lineIndex - noteLineIndex) × lineDistance`.

## Behavior

**Before**: Moving the cursor beyond the last measure showed no preview.

**After**: A shadow note with staff lines appears, showing exactly where the note will be placed.

## Technical Details

- Staff lines are drawn only when the cursor is beyond the measure's bounding box width
- Lines use the shadow note's color for consistency
- Line spacing and thickness match the staff's configuration
- Supports different staff types (5-line, 1-line, tablature)
- Ledger lines still appear for notes outside the staff range

## Testing

Tested scenarios include:
- Moving cursor beyond last measure at various vertical positions
- Different note durations and accidentals
- Multiple staff types (standard, percussion, tablature)
- Regression testing: existing behavior within measures unchanged
- Multiple staves and systems

## Compatibility

- ✅ No breaking changes to existing functionality
- ✅ Backward compatible with all existing code
- ✅ No new dependencies introduced
- ✅ Security checks passed (CodeQL)

## Files Modified

- `src/engraving/dom/score.cpp` - Position detection logic
- `src/engraving/dom/shadownote.h` - Staff lines flag
- `src/notation/internal/notationinteraction.cpp` - Beyond-measure detection
- `src/engraving/rendering/score/tdraw.cpp` - Staff line rendering

---

Resolves the issue by providing clear visual feedback for note placement beyond the last measure, improving the user experience in note input mode.

